From: Louis JULIEN <louis69600@laposte.net>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btusb: mediatek: initialise btmtk_data USB fields

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/linux/+bug/XXXXXXX

The 6.8.0-139 backport of the upstream series

  Bluetooth: btmtk: move btusb_mtk_hci_wmt_sync to btmtk.c

moved the MediaTek WMT handshake from btusb.c into btmtk.c. The moved
code reads the USB interface, device and control anchor from the btmtk
private area of hci_dev (hci_get_priv), but the corresponding hunk that
populates those fields in btusb_mtk_setup() was not carried across.

btusb_mtk_setup() sets only ->dev_id and ->reset_sync, leaving ->intf,
->udev and ->ctrl_anchor NULL. btmtk_usb_hci_wmt_sync() then calls
usb_autopm_get_interface(data->intf) with a NULL pointer during firmware
setup, oopsing in __pm_runtime_resume:

  BUG: kernel NULL pointer dereference, address: 0000000000000219
  RIP: 0010:__pm_runtime_resume+0x1b/0x80
  Call Trace:
   usb_autopm_get_interface+0x1d/0x60
   btmtk_usb_hci_wmt_sync+0xa9/0x2e0   [btmtk]
   btmtk_setup_firmware_79xx+0x1c7/0x360 [btmtk]
   btusb_mtk_setup+0x453/0x610         [btusb]
   hci_dev_setup_sync+0x6c/0x430       [bluetooth]
   hci_dev_open_sync+0xb1/0x350        [bluetooth]
   hci_power_on+0x50/0x210             [bluetooth]

The kworker exits with irqs disabled, firmware setup never completes and
the controller is left DOWN INIT with BD_ADDR 00:00:00:00:00:00, so no
Bluetooth adapter is usable on the machine.

Restore the missing assignments, matching upstream btusb_mtk_setup().

Reported-and-tested-by: Louis JULIEN <louis69600@laposte.net>
Signed-off-by: Louis JULIEN <louis69600@laposte.net>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
@@ -2975,6 +2975,9 @@ static int btusb_mtk_setup(struct hci_de
 	mediatek = hci_get_priv(hdev);
 	mediatek->dev_id = dev_id;
 	mediatek->reset_sync = btusb_mtk_reset;
+	mediatek->intf = data->intf;
+	mediatek->udev = data->udev;
+	mediatek->ctrl_anchor = &data->ctrl_anchor;
 
 	err = btmtk_register_coredump(hdev, btusb_driver.name, fw_version);
 	if (err < 0)
-- 
2.43.0
